Model uncertainty is estimated using Statistical Ensembling. The statistical ensemble technique trains several identical models and finds averages and deviations of the prediction. This method estimates uncertainty purely based on the trained model. Additionally, this also helps with desensitizing ARCliDS to the noise associated with the stochastic optimization algorithm used by NNs. NNs utilize a large number of randomly initiated weights and as a result, learned weights are different from model to model32. ARCliDS presents the average prediction \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
